---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../../site/config';
---

<Base
  title="Hermes Agent privacy policy"
  description="How Hermes Agent, a private single-user automation agent, accesses and stores data."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Hermes Agent', path: '/hermes' },
    { name: 'Privacy', path: '/hermes/privacy' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <header>
      <p class="legal-page__eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Hermes Agent privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-page__updated">Last updated 21 October 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-page__content">
      <p>
        Hermes Agent is a private automation agent with exactly one user: me, Hamish Burke. It is
        not offered to the public, has no sign-up, and is not installed on anyone else's machine.
        This policy explains what it can access, where that data lives, who can see it, and how
        that access is withdrawn.
      </p>

      <section aria-labelledby="operator">
        <h2 id="operator">Who operates it</h2>
        <p>
          Hamish Burke, Wellington, New Zealand. Contact
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. There is no company, no other
          account holder, and no other user.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="access">
        <h2 id="access">What it can access, and why</h2>
        <p>
          Access is granted by me, to myself, through Google's OAuth consent screen. Only the
          scopes I approve are granted, and each exists to do a task I asked for.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Gmail (read, send, modify):</strong> find and summarise email I ask about, draft replies, and send messages I have approved.</li>
          <li><strong>Calendar:</strong> read my schedule to plan my day, and create or move events I ask for.</li>
          <li><strong>Drive, Docs, Sheets:</strong> read and edit files I point it at, and create documents on my instruction.</li>
          <li><strong>Contacts:</strong> resolve who an email is from or to, so it addresses the right person.</li>
          <li><strong>Tasks:</strong> add, complete and list my own task items.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>It does not access anything outside these scopes, and does not read other people's accounts.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="storage">
        <h2 id="storage">Where the data lives</h2>
        <p>
          On my own laptop, in local files only I can read. There is no Hermes server, no hosted
          backend, and no cloud database holding this data. Nothing is sold, rented, or shared with
          advertisers or data brokers, and nothing is used to train machine-learning models.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="third-parties">
        <h2 id="third-parties">Third parties</h2>
        <p>
          To produce answers, the agent sends the specific text needed for a task to a
          large-language-model provider under my own account, in the same way I would send it to a
          search engine. It uses no analytics or tracking services and no advertiser SDKs. Where a
          task needs another service, only the minimum needed for that task is sent.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="google-policy">
        <h2 id="google-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</h2>
        <p>
          Hermes Agent's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
          <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener">
            Google API Services User Data Policy
          </a>, including the Limited Use requirements. Google user data is not used for advertising,
          is not sold, is not used to develop, improve or train generalised or non-personalised AI or
          machine-learning models, and is not read by humans except where I read my own data or where
          required for security or legal reasons.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="retention">
        <h2 id="retention">Retention and deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Data stays until I delete it. Local records can be removed at any time by deleting the
          files on my machine, and the OAuth grant can be revoked at any time at
          <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>,
          which immediately ends the agent's access.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="security">
        <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
        <p>
          OAuth tokens are stored locally with file permissions restricted to my user account. The
          machine is protected by its own login and disk encryption. No credentials are shared with,
          or stored by, any third party.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="changes">
        <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it. Because there is one user,
          there is nobody else to notify.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
